    "scope": "One exact-rational static layout/count feasibility check on existing TightUp8, not an implemented cache or proof of managed pixels/performance/whole peak. Prefix writes are disjoint from workspace; workspace must retire before tail writes, with views unwound and tail/source/result fully materialized. Actual no-alias/CT/refusal/independent lifetime/tinyalpha correctness and complete timing remain required.",
    "continuation": "Current confirmed~976usgap and dominant actual kernel justify a bounded architectural prototype, not merge. Share original horizontal preparation/publication/repair, use one admitted operation and existing output capacity, return to same strip scheduler only for the tail after full-row workspace views unwind. Preserve all arithmetic order, thresholds/halves/markers and exact replay. No fixture specialization, general cache/session or hidden managed setup. Extra L2 traffic, prefix/tail overlap recomputation and complexity may outweigh removed work; judge full encodes with memory/simplification and retain adverse points. Byte-first stage can temporarily duplicate scheduling; accepted end state should share geometry/lifetimes and retain typed kernels. No broader numerical policy change."
